kernel 5.4: quiet the vendor charger, fuel gauge, WCN and watchdog drivers' periodic log lines (issue #68)

By AgentFan0315 (https://github.com/AgentFan0315/f50-openwrt, kernel/patches/logspam-quiet.patch), GPL-2.0 like the
code it changes. Each line only changes the printk level to debug; CONFIG_DYNAMIC_DEBUG is on, so any of them comes
back with `echo 'file <file> +p' > /sys/kernel/debug/dynamic_debug/control`.
Left out of the original: the WCN_INFO macro in sprdwcn/include/wcn_dbg.h (every WCN info line, including the
start_marlin/stop_marlin power timeline that FINDINGS 31n/14b were read from) and charger-manager's two
"battery overheat or cold" warnings (the only record of a JEITA charging stop on the U30 Air).

